3. Install Python on Ubuntu

Open your Ubuntu VM.

Step1: First check whether Python is already installed:

python3 --version

Then:

which python3

Example:

/usr/bin/python3

Also check pip:

python3 -m pip --version

If pip isn't installed:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3-pip python3-venv -y

Then:

python3 --version
python3 -m pip --version

Step2: Create your Python practice directory

Let's keep all your work organized.

mkdir -p ~/python-linux-admin
cd ~/python-linux-admin

Create your first Python file:

nano hello.py

Put:

print("Hello Linux Admin")

Save.

Run:

python3 hello.py

Output:

Hello Linux Admin

Congratulations — you've executed your first Python automation script.
